<main class="page-main-with-hero corporate-volunteering-main">
  <!-- Place the Corporate Volunteering image in the same full-width hero position as the Volunteer page. -->
  <section class="page-hero-top corporate-volunteering-hero" aria-label="Corporate volunteering page hero image">
    <img src="/images/2024/11/sri-sathya-sai-BKFA-0044.jpg" alt="Clean birth kit boxes at a corporate volunteering event">
  </section>

  <div class="page-body-with-sidebar">
    <%- include('partials/getInvolvedSideMenu') %>

    <div class="page-content corporate-volunteering-page">
      <!-- Keep Corporate Volunteering in the same sidebar-and-content card layout as the Volunteer page. -->
      <section class="cv-intro">
      <h1>Increase Impact through Workplace Giving</h1>
      <h3>Your Company Can Support Safer Births Through Employee Matching Gifts, Payroll Giving, and Volunteering activities.</h3>

      <p>
        Every donation to Birthing Kit Foundation Australia helps create safer birthing environments for women, girls, and newborns in vulnerable communities. What many supporters don’t realise that their employer may offer programs that double, boost, or
        automate their generosity. They also may have volunteer programs that make donations supporting their volunteering activities. Making it easier than ever to create life‑changing impact.
      </p>

      <p>
        Here’s how you can make your support go even further.
      </p>

      <h2>Employee Matching Gifts</h2>

      <p>
        Many Australian and international employers offer Matching Gift Programs, where they match donations made by their staff.
      </p>

      <p>This could mean:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Your $50 donation becomes $100.</li>
        <li>Your $200 donation becomes $400.</li>
        <li>Your impact on maternal health is instantly multiplied.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        Matching gifts help BKFA reach more women and girls, supply more clean birthing kits, provide further sustainability through education and strengthen our global partnerships. It’s one of the simplest ways to increase your impact with BKFA without spending extra.
      </p>

      <p><strong>How to get started:</strong></p>
      <ol>
        <li>Check with your management to see if your employer offers donation matching.</li>
        <li>Submit your BKFA donation receipt through your workplace giving portal or HR system. BKFA is registered with most major portals including Benevity, Good2Give, Global Giving, MyCause, Charities Aid Foundation, YourCause, Double the Donation, Goodstack and Good Company amongst others.</li>
        <li>Your employer sends the matched funds directly to BKFA.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Payroll Giving</h2>
      <p>
        Payroll Giving allows Individuals to pledge regular donations to BKFA directly from their pre‑tax salary. It’s a simple, tax‑effective way to support BKFA’s work all year round.
      </p>

      <ol>
        <li>Effortless: Set it up and donations are made automatically each pay cycle.</li>
        <li>Tax‑effective: Donations come from your pre‑tax income, giving you an immediate tax benefit. BKFA has Deductable Gift Recipient (DGR1) status in Australia and hold a Maternal Health Fund registration internationally.</li>
        <li>Sustainable impact: Regular giving helps BKFA plan, strengthen programs, increase education and respond to emerging needs.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        Many employers will also match Payroll Giving donations.
      </p>

      <p>How to get started:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Contact your HR or payroll team and nominate BKFA as your chosen charity.</li>
        <li>Choose the amount you’d like to give each pay cycle.</li>
        <li>Your donation begins automatically — creating safer births every single pay period.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Paid Volunteering Activities</h2>

      <p>
        Many More employers now offer Paid Volunteer Leave, and for many large companies it is part of their ESG and CSR mandates. These give staff the opportunity to volunteer during work hours while still being paid. BKFA’s Birthing Kit Assembly Days are an ideal activity for teams using
        paid volunteering time and support their company Volunteering Activities.
      </p>

      <p>Why paid volunteering matters:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Employees give their time without losing income.</li>
        <li>Teams bond through meaningful, hands‑on activity.</li>
        <li>Organisations demonstrate real commitment to social impact.</li>
        <li>Every hour volunteered directly contributes to safer births worldwide.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        Whether your team volunteers onsite at your workplace as part of their company objectives, or joins a community Assembly Day, employees can utilise their passion to assist BKFA utilising the philanthropy of their organisation.
        BKFA publish locations that are seeking volunteers for assembly days on their website. Paid volunteering hours can be used to assemble clean birthing kits that support women in low‑resource settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Support Creates Real Change</h2>
      <p>Whether you give through matching gifts, payroll giving, volunteering your time, or a one‑off donation, your generosity helps BKFA:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Distribute clean birthing kits to women in low‑resource settings.</li>
        <li>Support global partners delivering maternal health programs.</li>
        <li>Support global partners in education promoting further sustainable change.</li>
        <li>Reduce infection, complications, and preventable deaths during childbirth.</li>
        <li>Empower communities with safer, more dignified birthing environments.</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="cv-tagline">
        Together, we can ensure more women and girls have access to a clean and safe birth wherever they may live.
      </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

